From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Attach the Broadcast RGB property

dw-hdmi always sends RGB in the quantization range that CTA-861 makes
the default for the mode: limited for every CTA mode on an HDMI sink,
full otherwise. Sinks that ignore the AVI InfoFrame quantization range
then crush or wash out the picture, and userspace has no way to
override it, unlike on other HDMI drivers.

Attach the "Broadcast RGB" property and take the range from it, with
Automatic keeping the current behaviour. The range is applied by the
CSC and signalled in the AVI InfoFrame only on a mode set, so force
one when the property changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index d3a9ddc..cf7df73 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2401,9 +2401,19 @@ static int dw_hdmi_setup(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi,
 	if (hdmi->hdmi_data.enc_out_bus_format == MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED)
 		hdmi->hdmi_data.enc_out_bus_format = MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24;
 
-	hdmi->hdmi_data.rgb_limited_range = hdmi->sink_is_hdmi &&
-		drm_default_rgb_quant_range(mode) ==
-		HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_LIMITED;
+	switch (connector->state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb) {
+	case DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_FULL:
+		hdmi->hdmi_data.rgb_limited_range = false;
+		break;
+	case DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_LIMITED:
+		hdmi->hdmi_data.rgb_limited_range = true;
+		break;
+	default:
+		hdmi->hdmi_data.rgb_limited_range = hdmi->sink_is_hdmi &&
+			drm_default_rgb_quant_range(mode) ==
+			HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_LIMITED;
+		break;
+	}
 
 	hdmi->hdmi_data.pix_repet_factor = 0;
 	hdmi->hdmi_data.hdcp_enable = 0;
@@ -2679,7 +2689,8 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_atomic_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	 * the display engine may convert to a different YCbCr encoding.
 	 */
 	if (!drm_connector_atomic_hdr_metadata_equal(old_state, new_state) ||
-	    old_state->colorspace != new_state->colorspace) {
+	    old_state->colorspace != new_state->colorspace ||
+	    old_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb != new_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb) {
 		crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state, crtc);
 		if (IS_ERR(crtc_state))
 			return PTR_ERR(crtc_state);
@@ -2747,6 +2758,7 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_create(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi)
 	drm_atomic_helper_connector_reset(connector);
 
 	drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property(connector, 8, 16);
+	drm_connector_attach_broadcast_rgb_property(connector);
 
 	/*
 	 * The output format is only negotiated when a bridge in front of
